---
import Site from "../layouts/Site.astro";
---

<Site
  title="Pricing"
  description="Planned Runstead launch pricing: one project free, or up to ten projects with Runstead Pro for $15 per month."
>
  <section class="page wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Planned launch pricing</p>
    <h1>Start with one project.</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      The same workflow tools on both plans. Choose how many projects you need
      on your machine.
    </p>
    <div class="cards">
      <article class="card">
        <h2>Free</h2>
        <div class="price">$0</div>
        <ul>
          <li>One project</li>
          <li>Visual workflows and YAML</li>
          <li>Schedules, history, and notifications</li>
          <li>AI tasks, MCP, and API access</li>
          <li>No Runstead account required</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="button secondary" href="/docs/">
          Explore Runstead
        </a>
      </article>
      <article class="card pro">
        <h2>Pro</h2>
        <div class="price">
          $15 <span>/ month · USD</span>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>Up to ten projects</li>
          <li>Every feature in Free</li>
          <li>Separate workflows, logs, and secrets per project</li>
          <li>Subscription managed through Dagu Cloud</li>
          <li>Existing projects keep running if Pro lapses</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="fine">Purchase will be available with the public launch.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Bring your own tools</h2>
      <p>
        AI provider usage, third-party subscriptions, and infrastructure costs
        are separate. Runstead does not include AI credits or a hosted computer
        to run your workflows.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/docs/ai/">Learn how AI tasks connect →</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Site>
